  "difficulty": 4,
  "marks": 3,
  "estimatedSeconds": 270,
  "stem": "The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = \\dfrac{2x + 3}{x - 2}$ for $x \\neq 2$. Show that $ff(x) = x$, and state what this tells you about $f^{-1}$.",
  "answerSpec": {
   "markScheme": {
    "points": [
     {
      "id": "p1",
      "description": "M1 substitutes $f(x)$ into $f$: $\\dfrac{2\\left(\\frac{2x + 3}{x - 2}\\right) + 3}{\\frac{2x + 3}{x - 2} - 2}$",
      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p2",
      "description": "A1 simplifies numerator to $\\frac{7x}{x - 2}$ and denominator to $\\frac{7}{x - 2}$, giving $x$",
      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p3",
      "description": "B1 concludes $f^{-1} = f$ (f is self-inverse)",
      "marks": 1
     }
    ]
   },
   "modelAnswer": "$$\nff(x) = \\frac{2\\left(\\frac{2x + 3}{x - 2}\\right) + 3}{\\frac{2x + 3}{x - 2} - 2} = \\frac{\\frac{4x + 6 + 3x - 6}{x - 2}}{\\frac{2x + 3 - 2x + 4}{x - 2}} = \\frac{7x}{7} = x\n$$\nSince applying $f$ twice returns $x$, $f$ undoes itself: $f^{-1}(x) = f(x) = \\dfrac{2x + 3}{x - 2}$."
  },
  "markingMode": "MANUAL",
  "explanation": "Multiply numerator and denominator by $(x - 2)$ to clear the inner fractions; the result is $\\frac{7x}{7} = x$.",
